B3 
Which input broke your first version: Inputs with leading,
trailing, or multiple consecutive spaces between names (such as '  ana   uwase  ' or '   ') broke the first version.

What you changed: 
Originally, using fullName.split(' ') produced empty strings ('') for extra spaces,
which caused a RangeError when trying to access index [0]. Adding .trim() to remove outer spaces, 
checking if (cleaned.isEmpty) return '';, and splitting with a regular expression RegExp(r'\s+') instead of a single space ' ' grouped consecutive 
spaces together and fixed the crash.
