  CORRECT ONE
  1. C becouse grades 85 above 50 and we go from top to bottom .
  2.RangeError (index): Invalid value: Not in inclusive range 0..4: 5, because On the very first iteration (i = 0), word[word.length - i]
    tries to access index 5 - 0 = 5, which is out of bounds for a 5-character string whose valid indices are 0 through 4.
  3. 
  String grade(int mark) {
  if (mark >= 80) {
    return 'A';
  } else if (mark >= 70) {
    return 'B';
  } else if (mark >= 50) {
    return 'C';
  }
  return 'F';
}

bool isPalindrome(String word) {
  String clean = word.toLowerCase();
  int i = 0;
  while (i < clean.length) {
    if (clean[i] != clean[clean.length - 1 - i]) return false;
    i++;
  }
  return true;
}
Choice: true
Justification: In everyday usage, a palindrome depends on the sequence of letters in a word rather than whether the first letter is capitalized
at the start of a sentence. Converting the string to lowercase (word.toLowerCase()) before comparing characters ensures that 'Level' 
is recognized as the same word backward and forward without rejecting valid capitalized inputs.

