PARTG 

1. Three Errors / Wrong Outputs Encountered


Error 1: initials() returning an empty string ('')

• Exact Error / Wrong Output:
'' (printed an empty line instead of S.M.E.)
• Line It Came From:
List<String> words = strimmed.split(''); and if (word.isEmpty) inside initials() (dart_basics.dart)
• What Caused It:
Calling .split('') without a space between the quotes split the name into individual letters instead of words, and checking if (word.isEmpty) only ran when a string had zero characters.
• How I Fixed It:
I changed .split('') to .split(' ') so it splits on spaces, and changed if (word.isEmpty) to if (word.isNotEmpty) so it skips extra spaces and extracts the first letter of each word.

Error 2: drawTriangle() printing numbers on separate lines in an infinite loop

• Exact Error / Wrong Output:
6
*
5
*
4
*
• Line It Came From:
int star = height--; print(star); print('*'); inside drawTriangle() (dart_basics.dart)
• What Caused It:
I decremented and printed height inside the loop, called print('*') on every single character instead of building one string per row, omitted leading spaces (height - row), and forgot to increment row++ and column++.
• How I Fixed It:
I built a String line = ''; for each row, added a while loop for height - row leading spaces before adding the * or # symbols, printed line once at the end of each row, and added space++, column++, and row++.

Error 3: isPalindrome('level') crashing with a RangeError

• Exact Error / Wrong Output:
Unhandled exception: RangeError (index): Invalid value: Not in inclusive range 0..4: 5
• Line It Came From:
if (word[i] != word[word.length - i]) return false; inside isPalindrome() (Part E)
• What Caused It:
On the first iteration (i = 0), word.length - i evaluated to 5 - 0 = 5, which is out of bounds because Dart string indices run from 0 to length - 1 (0 to 4).
• How I Fixed It:
I converted the input to lowercase (String clean = word.toLowerCase();) and changed word[word.length - i] to clean[clean.length - 1 - i] so indexing starts at the last valid character (4) and moves backward safely.

2. Reflection: Which Question Took the Longest, and Why?

Part F (momo_sim.dart) took me the longest to complete because it required combining five separate functions (momoFee, formatRwf, isValidPin, sendMoney, and buyAirtime) while strictly 
using while loops everywhere instead of for loops or external formatting libraries. Writing the logic in formatRwf to insert commas every three digits from right to left and testing edge cases—such as
 negative amounts, invalid PINs, and balance checks that include transaction fees—took careful planning and debugging.